# The initramfs overlay

Whatever is in this directory is merged into the early userspace the kernel
unpacks: the *contents* map to that archive's root, so `initramfs/init` becomes
`/init` and replaces what the packages put there. Directories are merged; files
and symlinks overwrite.

## init

`init` is the script the kernel runs as pid 1 on the ramfs. It mounts the
pseudo-filesystems, mounts the filesystem the command line names with `root=`,
moves the mounts onto it and `switch_root`s into `/sbin/init`.

It lives here rather than in a Rust string in `xtask`, so editing it is editing
a shell script. It must stay executable - the kernel execs it - and the archive
carries the mode it has in this tree.

Two things are worth knowing when changing it:

* Anything created *before* `switch_root` disappears with the ramfs; anything
  mounted onto the new root survives. That is why the script makes `/sysroot/tmp`
  and friends and then mounts onto them.
* `mount -t devpts devpts /sysroot/dev/pts` is not optional. Without it every
  `openpty` in the real system fails with ENOENT - which is how a `doas` or a
  nested shell reports "unable to allocate pty".

## An extra mount at boot

```sh
# initramfs/etc/extra-mount.sh
#!/bin/sh
mount -t tmpfs tmpfs /tmp
```
